<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    package="com.unity3d.player"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <!--
      P1-05: the AD_SERVICES_CONFIG removal directive that used to live here has been deleted.

        <meta-data tools:node="remove" android:name="android.adservices.AD_SERVICES_CONFIG"/>

      It was half of Google's own workaround for a manifest-merger conflict in Google Mobile Ads
      v8.6.0. The underlying issue was fixed in the GMA Android SDK 24.0.0; this project resolves
      play-services-ads 25.4.0, so the workaround is obsolete.

      What removing it did NOT do: restore any meta-data. All 90 resolved dependency manifests
      were checked and none declares AD_SERVICES_CONFIG - play-services-ads 25.4.0 and
      play-services-ads-api 25.4.0 included. The directive was inert, and the APK built without
      it contains the meta-data exactly as often as the APK built with it: zero times.

      It is removed because a directive that silently strips a meta-data nothing currently
      declares is a trap for later. The moment an SDK update or a re-added mediation adapter
      starts shipping AD_SERVICES_CONFIG, this line would have deleted it again with no error
      and no log line. Do not reintroduce it.
    -->

    <application>
        <activity android:name="com.unity3d.player.UnityPlayerActivity"
                  android:theme="@style/UnityThemeSelector">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
            <meta-data android:name="unityplayer.UnityActivity" android:value="true" />
        </activity>
    </application>
</manifest>
